---
description: SQL migration conventions
globs: ["src/kernel/migrations/*.sql"]
alwaysApply: false
---

- Migrations are ordered `NNNN_short_name.sql`, append-only: never edit or renumber a merged migration — write a new one.
- Each migration is idempotent-safe to re-run (`IF NOT EXISTS` where possible) and contains no data backfill mixed with DDL — separate migrations.
- Every table gets: `id` (text, kernel-generated), `created_at timestamptz not null default now()`; foreign keys are explicit.
- PII columns (phones, names, ids) are commented `-- pii` so log/export tooling can find them.
- Never DROP a column or table in the same release that stops writing it — deprecate first, drop a release later.
